  "description": "Prior approval for change of use to existing workshop (Class E) as 1 x bed single storey dwelling (Class C3) together with associated bin and cycle storage.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rApplication Form,\rInternal Daylight and Sunlight Assessment,\rPlanning Statement,\r1aPynt-D-001,\r1aPynt-D-002,\r1aPynt-D-003,\r1aPynt-D-004,\r1aPynt-D-005A,\r1aPynt-D-006,\r1aPynt-D-007,\r1aPynt-D-008,\r1aPynt-D-009,\r1aPynt-D-010,\r1aPynt-D-100,\r1aPynt-D-101.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, the proposed cycle store indicated within Drawing No. 1aPynt-D-005A and 1aPynt-D-009 shall have been fully provided on site. \r\rNotwithstanding the details shown within the 1aPynt-D-009, the cycle store hereby approved shall be fully secure and lockable. \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, the proposed bin store indicated within Drawing No. 1aPynt-D-005A and 1aPynt-D-010 shall have been fully provided on site. \r\rBins shall be provided in accordance with Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024).\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets.\r"
  ],
